    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Write each decimal as a sum of its non-zero place-value parts.\n(a) $8.263$\n(b) $4.009$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $8.263=8+0.2+0.06+0.003$\n(b) $4.009=4+0.009$\nThe tenths and hundredths have value $0$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write the decimal represented by $7+0.04+0.008$.",
        "solution_text": "There are $7$ ones, $0$ tenths, $4$ hundredths and $8$ thousandths.\n$7+0.04+0.008=7.048$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $6.754$:\n(a) Regroup it into a whole-number part and one decimal part.\n(b) Give a partition with three non-zero parts, using none of its standard parts $6$, $0.7$, $0.05$ or $0.004$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $6.754=6+0.754$\n(b) Combine the hundredths and thousandths, then regroup one whole with the tenths.\n$\\begin{aligned}6.754&=6+0.7+0.054\\\\&=5+1.7+0.054\\end{aligned}$\nThe three parts are non-zero and none is a standard part."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Find the missing part: $4.963=4+0.8+\\square$.",
        "solution_text": "$4.963=4+0.9+0.06+0.003$\n$0.9=0.8+0.1$\n$\\square=0.1+0.06+0.003$\n$\\square=0.163$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "What part does the digit $7$ contribute to $3.275$?",
        "solution_text": "The decimal digits represent $2$ tenths, $7$ hundredths and $5$ thousandths.\nThe $7$ is in the hundredths place, so its part is $0.07$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Is $2.608=2+0.5+0.108$ a correct partition? Give a reason.\n(b) A learner writes $2.608=2+0.6+0.08$. Correct the partition.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}2+0.5+0.108\\\\&=2+0.608\\\\&=2.608\\end{aligned}$\nYes, the parts total $2.608$.\n(b) The $8$ is in the thousandths place, so its part is $0.008$.\n$2.608=2+0.6+0.008$"
      }
    ],
